This is LeetCode 112 — Path Sum. Your solution uses DFS + Recursion.

1. Problem Description

You are given the root of a binary tree and an integer targetSum.

You need to determine whether there exists a root-to-leaf path such that the sum of all node values along that path is exactly equal to targetSum.

A leaf node is a node that has:

left == null
right == null
Example
        5
       / \
      4   8
     /   / \
    11  13  4
   /  \       \
  7    2       1

If:

targetSum = 22

There is a path:

5 → 4 → 11 → 2

Sum:

5 + 4 + 11 + 2 = 22

So the answer is:

true


Logic :

I used DFS with recursion. I maintain the remaining target sum while traversing from the root toward the leaf. At each node, I subtract the current node's value from the target sum. 
When I reach a leaf node, I check whether the remaining target sum is zero. If it is zero, we found a valid root-to-leaf path.
Otherwise, I recursively search both the left and right subtrees, and return true if either subtree contains a valid path


Code:

class Solution {
    public boolean hasPathSum(TreeNode root, int targetSum) {
        if(root==null){
            return false;
        }
        targetSum-=root.val;
        if(root.left==null && root.right==null){
            return targetSum==0;
        }
        return hasPathSum(root.left,targetSum) || hasPathSum(root.right,targetSum);
    }
}
